IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mla-levy`

-- Medicare Levy Act 1986 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the taxpayer: ss 3, 3A, 6(1), 7(1)-(2), 8, 8B-8D, 9.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case or an ATO publication. Fixtures are generated by scratchpad gen_medicare-levy-act-1986_baseline.py; expected
-- results were written by hand from the deposited text and from the formulas transcribed by hand in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03351.formulas.md.
--
-- The lives (workbench scenarios/au/wa): chloe c045 (2024-10-20), first return, for 2023-24, taxable income $27,500; the
-- scenario notes "Medicare levy nil under the threshold". chloe c048 (2025-10-25), second return, for 2024-25, taxable income
-- $71,500; the scenario records "medicare_levy": 1430. Chloe's hospital cover is not stated in the scenario: she is ASSUMED to
-- hold none, and her income for surcharge purposes is ASSUMED equal to her taxable income.
--
-- Both of Chloe's years are before 2025-26, the year the deposited figures are taken to be for (an INFERENCE: see the module
-- header), so the whole answer for each is `Not in the deposited text`; each is also read under the deposited figures.
--
-- Tier thresholds: every fixture uses $90,000 / $105,000 / $140,000, the Private Health Insurance Act s 22-35 figures "for the
-- 2021-22 and 2022-23 financial year", as ASSUMED stand-ins for the indexed figures (not deposited). Indexing never lowers them
-- (s 22-45(3), (3A)), so an income at or under $90,000 is under the singles tier 1 threshold in every later year too.
--
-- Agreement with ../../../income-tax-rates-act-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10 and
-- ../../../income-tax-assessment-act-1997/encodings/baseline-2026-10: same taxable incomes for c045 ($27,500) and c048
-- ($71,500); 2023-24 is outside the deposited text in all three; the levy is not part of their tax figures.

