§ `The year the figures are for`

#ASSERT `Does the deposited text give the figures for my year` 2025
#ASSERT NOT `Does the deposited text give the figures for my year` 2024

§ `ss 3, 6, 7 -- rate, thresholds, shading-in`

#ASSERT `What is the rate of levy`  EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `What is my threshold amount` FALSE EQUALS 28011
#ASSERT `What is my phase-in limit` FALSE EQUALS 35013
-- s 7(1): at or under the threshold amount, nil.
#ASSERT `Is my income under the threshold` 28011 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my income under the threshold` 28012 FALSE
-- s 7(2): $31,011 is $3,000 over $28,011: 10% is $300, less than 2% ($620.22).
#ASSERT `How much levy on my own income` 31011 FALSE EQUALS 300
-- $34,011: 10% of $6,000 is $600, less than $680.22.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $34,011` EQUALS (Amount 600)
-- A senior entitled to the s 160AAAA rebate: $44,000 is under $44,268 (phase-in limit $55,335); $49,268 is $5,000 over, so 10% = $500 < $985.36.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a senior on $44,000` EQUALS (Amount 0)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a senior on $49,268` EQUALS (Amount 500)

§ `chloe c045 -- first tax return, for 2023-24`

-- 2023-24 is before the deposited figures. The s 6 rate alone: 2% of $27,500 = $550.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `Chloe, 2023-24 return (c045)` EQUALS `Not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `How much surcharge do I pay` `Chloe, 2023-24 return (c045)` EQUALS `Not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `How much is the levy at the full rate` 27500 EQUALS 550
-- Read under the deposited figures: $27,500 does not exceed $28,011, so nil (s 7(1)); no surcharge, $27,500 is under
-- the singles tier 1 threshold. Whether it was under the 2023-24 threshold cannot be checked from this deposit.
#ASSERT `Is my income under the threshold` 27500 FALSE
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `Chloe's $27,500 read under the deposited figures` EQUALS (Amount 0)

§ `chloe c048 -- second return, 2024-25`

-- 2024-25 is before the deposited figures. The s 6 rate alone: 2% of $71,500 = $1,430, the scenario's figure.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `Chloe, 2024-25 return (c048)` EQUALS `Not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `How much is the levy at the full rate` 71500 EQUALS 1430
-- Read under the deposited figures: above the $35,013 phase-in limit, so the full $1,430. No hospital cover, but $71,500
-- is under the singles tier 1 threshold ($90,000 or more in any year), so no surcharge.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `Chloe's $71,500 read under the deposited figures` EQUALS (Amount 1430)
#ASSERT NOT `Must I pay the surcharge` `Chloe's $71,500 read under the deposited figures`
#ASSERT `Which income tier am I in` `Chloe's $71,500 read under the deposited figures` EQUALS `not above the tier 1 threshold`

§ `s 3(3) -- married on the last day`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I married on the last day of the year` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I married on the last day of the year` FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 8 -- families`

-- Married, $30,000 + $15,000 = $45,000, not over $47,238: nil.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a couple on $30,000 and $15,000` EQUALS (Amount 0)
-- Two children: $47,238 + 2 x $4,338 = $55,914; $54,000 is under it, so nil although $40,000 alone would pay $800.
#ASSERT `What is my family income threshold` `a couple with 2 children on $40,000 and $14,000` EQUALS 55914
#ASSERT `Is our family income under the family threshold` `a couple with 2 children on $40,000 and $14,000`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a couple with 2 children on $40,000 and $14,000` EQUALS (Amount 0)
-- Living separately and apart: not married (s 3(3)(a)), no family case, $800.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in the family case` `a couple who live apart, on $40,000 and $14,000`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a couple who live apart, on $40,000 and $14,000` EQUALS (Amount 800)
-- Single parent: s 8(6) counts only the child for whom family tax benefit was payable: $47,238 + $4,338 = $51,576.
#ASSERT `What is my family income threshold` `a single parent of 2 on $50,000, family tax benefit for 1` EQUALS 51576
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single parent of 2 on $50,000, family tax benefit for 1` EQUALS (Amount 0)
-- No family tax benefit: $47,238; $50,000 is over it by $2,762. s 8(2): 2% of $47,238 = $944.76, less 0.08 x $2,762 =
-- $220.96, gives $723.80. Levy $1,000 less $723.80 = $276.20 -- which is 10% of the $2,762 excess. Not married: no s 8(3).
#ASSERT `What is my family income threshold` `a single parent of 2 on $50,000, no family tax benefit` EQUALS 47238
#ASSERT `What is my s 8(2) reduction amount` `a single parent of 2 on $50,000, no family tax benefit` EQUALS 723.8
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single parent of 2 on $50,000, no family tax benefit` EQUALS (Amount 276.2)
-- s 8(3): family income $50,000, threshold $47,238: the s 8(2) reduction is $723.80 (as above). Spouse liable, so less
-- $723.80 x 30,000 / 50,000 = $434.28, leaving $289.52. My own levy is nil ($20,000 is under the threshold), so s 8(4)
-- passes the whole $289.52 to my spouse.
#ASSERT `By how much is my levy reduced for my family` `a married person on $20,000, spouse liable on $30,000` EQUALS 289.52
#ASSERT `By how much is my spouse's levy reduced` `a married person on $20,000, spouse liable on $30,000` EQUALS 289.52
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a married person on $20,000, spouse liable on $30,000` EQUALS (Amount 0)
-- $36,000 each: family income $72,000 is $24,762 over $47,238; 0.08 x $24,762 = $1,980.96 exceeds $944.76, so the
-- s 8(2) formula gives nothing (if any). Own levy $720 stands; nothing passes to the spouse.
#ASSERT `What is my s 8(2) reduction amount` `a married person on $36,000, spouse liable on $36,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `By how much is my levy reduced for my family` `a married person on $36,000, spouse liable on $36,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `By how much is my spouse's levy reduced` `a married person on $36,000, spouse liable on $36,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a married person on $36,000, spouse liable on $36,000` EQUALS (Amount 720)
-- s 3(3)(b): a spouse who died in the year is treated as a spouse on the last day: $45,000 family income, nil.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a widow on $30,000 whose husband died in March on $15,000` EQUALS (Amount 0)

§ `s 9 -- prescribed for part of the year`

-- $1,000 less 73/365 of it = $800.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $50,000, prescribed for 73 days` EQUALS (Amount 800)

§ `s 3(5) -- private patient hospital cover`

#ASSERT `Does my policy count as hospital cover` TRUE TRUE TRUE 750
#ASSERT NOT `Does my policy count as hospital cover` TRUE TRUE TRUE 751
#ASSERT `Does my policy count as hospital cover` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1500

§ `ss 3A, 8B-8D -- the surcharge`

-- s 8B, tier 1 ($100,000 > $90,000, not > $105,000): 1% = $1,000, on top of $2,000.
#ASSERT `Which income tier am I in` `a single person on $100,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS `a tier 1 earner`
#ASSERT `How much surcharge do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS (Amount 1000)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS (Amount 3000)
-- Tier 2: 1.25% of $120,000 = $1,500; total $3,900. Tier 3: 1.5% of $150,000 = $2,250; total $5,250.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $120,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS (Amount 3900)
#ASSERT `Which income tier am I in` `a single person on $150,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS `a tier 3 earner`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $150,000 without hospital cover` EQUALS (Amount 5250)
-- Covered all year: no surcharge, $3,000.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I pay the surcharge` `a single person on $150,000 with hospital cover`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $150,000 with hospital cover` EQUALS (Amount 3000)
-- Tested on income for surcharge purposes ($95,000), charged on taxable income: 1% of $85,000 = $850; total $2,550.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $85,000 with $95,000 for surcharge purposes` EQUALS (Amount 2550)
-- s 8D: $190,000 combined > $180,000 (double $90,000); own $100,000 > $28,011; families table tier 1 (not > $210,000):
-- 1% = $1,000, on top of $2,000 (family income $190,000 is far above the family threshold: s 8(2) reduction nil).
#ASSERT `Which surcharge section applies to me` `a married person on $100,000, spouse $90,000, no cover` EQUALS `section 8D -- married`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a married person on $100,000, spouse $90,000, no cover` EQUALS (Amount 3000)
-- s 8D(3)(c): own $20,000 does not exceed $28,011, so no surcharge although the couple's $220,000 is over the line.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my income above the surcharge line` `a married person on $20,000, spouse $200,000, no cover`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a married person on $20,000, spouse $200,000, no cover` EQUALS (Amount 0)
-- s 8C: family tier 1 = $180,000 + the (input, ASSUMED) child increase $1,500 = $181,500. $170,000 is under it: $3,400.
-- $185,000 is over it; families table tier 1 (not over $211,500): 1% = $1,850 on $3,700 = $5,550.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single parent on $170,000, no cover` EQUALS (Amount 3400)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single parent on $185,000, no cover` EQUALS (Amount 5550)
-- Part-year, s 8B(2)(b): (1% of $100,000) x 73 / 365 = $200, on top of $2,000.
#ASSERT `For how much of the year does the surcharge section apply` `a single person on $100,000 without cover for 73 days` EQUALS `part of the year`
#ASSERT `Must I pay the surcharge` `a single person on $100,000 without cover for 73 days`
#ASSERT `How much surcharge do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 without cover for 73 days` EQUALS (Amount 200)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 without cover for 73 days` EQUALS (Amount 2200)
-- Tier 2 part-year, ss 8B(2)(b), (3): (1.25% of $120,000) x 146 / 365 = $1,500 x 0.4 = $600, on top of $2,400.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $120,000 without cover for 146 days` EQUALS (Amount 3000)
-- s 8D(4) for a person married all year: same income test as s 8D(3); (1% of $100,000) x 73 / 365 = $200.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge do I pay` `a married person on $100,000, spouse $90,000, no cover for 73 days` EQUALS (Amount 200)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a married person on $100,000, spouse $90,000, no cover for 73 days` EQUALS (Amount 2200)
-- Uncovered days and prescribed days in one year: their overlap is not asked, so those days are unknown.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 without cover for 73 days, prescribed for 30` EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
-- Married from January: s 8B or 8C before, s 8D after; the days under each section are not asked.
#ASSERT `Which surcharge section applies to me` `a person on $100,000 married from January, no cover` EQUALS `more than one section in the year`
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a person on $100,000 married from January, no cover` EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`

§ `Out of scope, and later years`

-- s 9A (lump sums in arrears) is not encoded.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $60,000 with a lump sum in arrears` EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
-- 2026-27: the deposited figures stand until amended: $2,000.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay` `a single person on $100,000 with cover, 2026-27` EQUALS (Amount 2000)
-- The simple question.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay, simply` 2025 100000 FALSE 90000 105000 140000 EQUALS (Amount 3000)
#ASSERT `How much Medicare levy do I pay, simply` 2024 71500 FALSE 90000 105000 140000 EQUALS `Not in the deposited text`
